{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L2389","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/types.ts:2389"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for cancelling an in-flight fetch, e.g. via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query.cancel()"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThey are carried on the "},{"type":"link","href":"../classes/CancelledError.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CancelledError"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that the cancelled fetch rejects with."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"property-revert\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"revert?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the query goes back to the state it had before the fetch started, instead of getting the cancellation error."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"property-silent\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"silent?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the cancellation error isn't surfaced, e.g. because another fetch replaces the cancelled one."}]}]]}],"headings":[{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/types.ts:2389](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L2389)\n\nOptions for cancelling an in-flight fetch, e.g. via `query.cancel()`.\nThey are carried on the [CancelledError](../classes/CancelledError.md) that the cancelled fetch rejects with.\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"property-revert\"></a> `revert?` | `boolean` | If `true`, the query goes back to the state it had before the fetch started, instead of getting the cancellation error. |\n| <a id=\"property-silent\"></a> `silent?` | `boolean` | If `true`, the cancellation error isn't surfaced, e.g. because another fetch replaces the cancelled one. |\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: CancelOptions\ntitle: CancelOptions\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/types.ts:2389](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L2389)\n\nOptions for cancelling an in-flight fetch, e.g. via `query.cancel()`.\nThey are carried on the [CancelledError](../classes/CancelledError.md) that the cancelled fetch rejects with.\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"property-revert\"></a> `revert?` | `boolean` | If `true`, the query goes back to the state it had before the fetch started, instead of getting the cancellation error. |\n| <a id=\"property-silent\"></a> `silent?` | `boolean` | If `true`, the cancellation error isn't surfaced, e.g. because another fetch replaces the cancelled one. |\n"}
